---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const siteTitle = 'Louis the History Goose';
const siteUrl = 'https://www.louisgoose.click/';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | Louis the History Goose" description="Privacy Policy for Louis the History Goose" robots="noindex, nofollow">
		<main class="privacy-policy">
			<div class="container">
				<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

				<p class="updated">
					Last updated: September 7, 2026
				</p>

				<section>
					<h2>1. Introduction</h2>

					<p>
						Welcome to <strong>{siteTitle}</strong> ({siteUrl}).
						We respect your privacy and are committed to protecting
						your personal data.
					</p>

					<p>
						This Privacy Policy explains what information may be
						collected when you visit our website, how that
						information is used, and what rights you have under
						applicable data protection laws, including the
						European Union General Data Protection Regulation
						(GDPR).
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>2. Data Controller</h2>

					<p>
						The data controller responsible for this website is:
					</p>

					<address>
						<strong>{siteTitle}</strong><br />
						Website: <a href={siteUrl}>{siteUrl}</a>
					</address>

					<p>
						If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or
						how your personal data is handled, please contact us
						using the contact information provided on our
						website's Impressum page.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>3. Information We Collect</h2>

					<p>
						We aim to collect only the information that is
						necessary for operating and improving the website.
					</p>

					<h3>Information you provide</h3>

					<p>
						If you voluntarily contact us, for example by email
						or through a contact form, we may receive information
						such as your name, email address, and the contents of
						your message.
					</p>

					<h3>Automatically collected information</h3>

					<p>
						When you visit the website, certain technical
						information may be processed automatically by the
						server or hosting provider. This may include your IP
						address, browser type, operating system, requested
						pages, date and time of access, and technical log
						information.
					</p>

					<p>
						This information may be processed for security,
						technical operation, troubleshooting, and abuse
						prevention.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>4. Legal Bases for Processing</h2>

					<p>
						Where the GDPR applies, personal data is processed
						based on one or more of the following legal bases:
					</p>

					<ul>
						<li>
							<strong>Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR:</strong> consent.
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR:</strong> processing
							necessary to perform a contract or take steps
							before entering into a contract.
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR:</strong> legitimate
							interests, such as maintaining website security
							and improving our services.
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR:</strong> compliance
							with legal obligations where applicable.
						</li>
					</ul>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>5. Hosting</h2>

					<p>
						This website may be hosted by a third-party hosting
						provider. When you access the website, the hosting
						provider may process technical information such as
						your IP address and server log data.
					</p>

					<p>
						This processing is generally necessary to provide
						the website securely and reliably and to detect and
						prevent technical attacks or misuse.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>6. Cookies</h2>

					<p>
						Our website may use cookies or similar technologies.
						Some cookies may be technically necessary for the
						website to function correctly.
					</p>

					<p>
						If we use analytics, advertising, affiliate tracking,
						or other technologies that are not strictly necessary,
						we will request consent where required by applicable
						law before activating those technologies.
					</p>

					<p>
						You can manage or withdraw your cookie preferences
						through the cookie consent mechanism provided on the
						website, where available.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>7. Analytics</h2>

					<p>
						We may use privacy-conscious analytics tools to
						understand how visitors use our website, such as which
						pages are visited and how users interact with the site.
					</p>

					<p>
						If analytics services that require consent are used,
						they will only be activated after obtaining the
						required consent.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>8. Affiliate Links</h2>

					<p>
						Some pages on <strong>{siteTitle}</strong> may contain
						affiliate links. If you click an affiliate link and
						make a purchase, we may receive a commission from the
						merchant or affiliate network.
					</p>

					<p>
						The price you pay is generally not increased because
						of an affiliate link.
					</p>

					<p>
						Affiliate networks and merchants may use cookies or
						other tracking technologies to attribute purchases
						and commissions. Where legally required, such
						technologies will only be used after obtaining your
						consent.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>9. Third-Party Services and Links</h2>

					<p>
						Our website may contain links to third-party websites,
						products, services, or platforms. Once you leave
						<strong>{siteTitle}</strong>, the privacy practices
						of those third parties are governed by their own
						privacy policies.
					</p>

					<p>
						We are not responsible for the privacy practices,
						content, or security of third-party websites.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>10. Data Retention</h2>

					<p>
						We retain personal data only for as long as necessary
						to fulfil the purposes for which it was collected,
						to comply with legal obligations, resolve disputes,
						and enforce our agreements where applicable.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>11. Your Rights Under the GDPR</h2>

					<p>
						If the GDPR applies to you, you may have the following
						rights:
					</p>

					<ul>
						<li>The right to access your personal data.</li>
						<li>The right to correct inaccurate data.</li>
						<li>The right to request deletion of your data.</li>
						<li>
							The right to restrict processing in certain
							circumstances.
						</li>
						<li>
							The right to object to certain processing,
							including processing based on legitimate
							interests.
						</li>
						<li>
							The right to data portability where applicable.
						</li>
						<li>
							The right to withdraw consent at any time where
							processing is based on consent.
						</li>
					</ul>

					<p>
						Withdrawing consent does not affect the lawfulness of
						processing carried out before the withdrawal.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>12. Right to Lodge a Complaint</h2>

					<p>
						You have the right to lodge a complaint with a data
						protection supervisory authority if you believe that
						your personal data is being processed unlawfully.
					</p>

					<p>
						In Germany, you can contact the competent data
						protection authority for your place of residence or
						work, or the authority responsible for the controller.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>13. Data Security</h2>

					<p>
						We use reasonable technical and organisational
						measures designed to protect personal data against
						loss, misuse, unauthorised access, disclosure, or
						destruction.
					</p>

					<p>
						However, no method of transmitting or storing
						information online can be guaranteed to be completely
						secure.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>14. Children's Privacy</h2>

					<p>
						Our website is not intentionally directed at children,
						and we do not knowingly collect personal information
						from children.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>15. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>

					<p>
						We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time
						to reflect changes to our website, services,
						technology, or legal requirements.
					</p>

					<p>
						The latest version will always be published on this
						page with the corresponding update date.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>16. Contact</h2>

					<p>
						If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or
						want to exercise your data protection rights, please
						contact us using the contact details provided on our
						website.
					</p>
				</section>
			</div>
		</main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.privacy-policy {
		padding: 5rem 1.5rem;
	}

	.container {
		max-width: 850px;
		margin: 0 auto;
	}

	h1 {
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}

	h2 {
		margin-top: 3rem;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	h3 {
		margin-top: 2rem;
	}

	p,
	li {
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	.updated {
		opacity: 0.7;
		margin-bottom: 3rem;
	}

	address {
		font-style: normal;
		line-height: 1.7;
		margin: 1.5rem 0;
	}

	a {
		text-decoration: underline;
	}
</style>